From 4b2983c6bbed48ef4c795cb47092cc96fccfe488 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:21:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): an absent rotary takes no angle word in fanuc and
 doosan-dnm

The RTCP arm block wrote A, B and C whatever the machine stated: on the
A+B tilthead `G00 X0 Y0 Z20 A30 B0 C0`. Angle words now name only the
rotaries in machine.rotaries; a turning letter of an absent rotary is
still refused by name (missingLetter runs first). doosan-dnm's RTCP
path is the same code and gets the same fix; the other posts refuse
tilted streams or write A only.

Pinned by the #926 recorded fanuc `rotary` golden (removed from
KNOWN_BUGS), fanuc_post::an_absent_rotary_takes_no_angle_word and
doosan_dnm_post::doosan_dnm_absent_rotary_takes_no_angle_word.

Fixes #997

